The {{nihongo|'''Suwa clan'''|諏訪氏|Suwa-shi}} was a Japanese clan which claimed descent from the [[Seiwa Genji]]. It was a powerful clan of [[Shinano Province]], particularly during the [[Sengoku period]], when it had frequent clashes with its neighbor in Kai, the [[Takeda clan]]. The Suwa served as Takeda retainers for some time, and after the fall of the Takeda, reemerged. The family entered the [[Edo period]] as [[daimyo]], and eventually came to rule the [[Suwa Domain]] of [[Shinano Province]].
